hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2971","Narrated to us Abdullah ibn Sa'eed al-Ashajj, narrated to us Abu Khalid — and he is Sulayman ibn Hayyan — on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Abdur-Rahman ibn al-Qasim, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha (RA), who said:\n\The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) departed on the last of his days when he prayed the Zuhr prayer"," then returned and stayed in Mina during the nights of the days of Tashreeq. He would stone the Jamrah when the sun had passed its zenith"," throwing seven small pebbles at each Jamrah. He would say 'Allahu Akbar' with each pebble"," and he would stand by the first and second Jamrah"," prolonging his standing and supplicating humbly. Then he would stone the third Jamrah but would not stand by it.\""\n\n**CHAPTER:**"""
